      "title": "Water seals stop vapour and fire travelling",
      "description": "Open drains take non-pressurised spills, leaks and rainwater from paved, curbed areas. Each drain hub connects through a liquid seal (P-trap or sealed catch basin) so flammable vapour and flame cannot travel through the drain network from one area to another; seals must be kept topped up. Oily water flows to a sump and on to an oil–water separator; the skimmer removes floating oil.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
